# Motion: Full, then a Standard game to a time-travel jump that creates a timeline, captured mid-animation:
# hover preview of the knight's moves (with a dashed arc to the other boards), the live arc to the hovered time-travel target,
# the new lane unfolding from its parent, the halo on the board the knight left, and the present column sliding on Submit.
# Settings layout: Settings (150,490); Display tab (880,172); Motion cycle (700,532); Back (125,25); Submit (841,90).
wait 20
click 150 490
wait 30
click 880 172
wait 20
click 700 532        # Motion: Reduced -> Full
wait 10
click 125 25
wait 30
mode standard
wait 120
clicksq 0 0 e2
wait 40
clicksq 0 0 e4
wait 60
click 841 90         # Submit: the present column slides to Black's board
wait 3
capture motion-slide-f3
wait 5
capture motion-slide-f8
wait 8
capture motion-slide-f16
wait 60
clicksq 0 1 e7
wait 40
clicksq 0 1 e5
wait 60
click 841 90
wait 90
move 700 700         # the pointer rests away from the boards, then comes to the knight: the preview starts after a short dwell
wait 5
hoversq 0 2 g1
wait 12
capture motion-preview-f12
wait 14
capture motion-preview-f26
clicksq 0 2 g1       # pick the knight up
wait 40
hoversq 0 0 g3       # a time-travel target two boards back: the arc grows towards it
wait 3
capture motion-livearc-f3
wait 4
capture motion-livearc-f7
wait 40
capture motion-livearc-settled
clicksq 0 0 g3       # the jump creates timeline L+1
wait 3
capture motion-lane-f3
wait 4
capture motion-lane-f7
wait 5
capture motion-lane-f12
wait 8
capture motion-lane-f20
wait 40
capture motion-lane-f60
wait 40
capture motion-lane-settled
